npc woodcutter 59.5 14.4 look=341 name="A Woodcutter" facing=left when=a1-c1-02 say="Sawed it through at first light. Took four of us.|Two of the lads went on into the Mirewood for oak. Not back yet.|Past here the trees have gone wrong. You'll see."

; The people out on a fine day: the farmer's wife in her yard, the miller by his mill, the farmer
; in his wheat, a girl picking flowers by the pond, the angler, two out walking in the meadow, and
; a traveller on the road.
npc farmwife 4.6 12.4 look=322 name="The Farmer's Wife" facing=down say="Eggs, milk or advice? The advice is free.|The windmill's been turning since my gran's day.|Wipe your boots if you're coming in."
npc miller 16 11.8 look=278 name="The Miller" facing=left say="Flour for the Rising Loaf, every morning.|Good wind today. The sails haven't stopped.|Don't stand under the sails. They don't stop for anyone."
npc farmer 10 23.6 look=311 name="The Farmer" facing=down wander=2 say="Wheat's in early. The sun's been kind.|The scarecrow does nothing. The crow likes him.|Walk round the field, not through it."
npc girl 19.4 22.6 look=188 name="A Girl" wander=3 say="I'm picking flowers for my mum.|There's a frog in the pond. He's called Sir Ribbit.|Are you going to the Mirewood? Mum says not to."
npc angler 27.6 27.6 look=257 name="An Angler" facing=left say="Shh. They're biting.|Caught a pike here once. This big. Bigger.|The stream comes down from the hills. Clean as anything."
npc walker-a 32.4 4.4 look=207 name="A Young Man" facing=right say="Lovely day for it.|We walk out to the oak every rest day.|She says the oak's older than the city. I believe her."
npc walker-b 34 4.6 look=228 name="A Young Woman" facing=left say="Don't mind him. He's in love with the oak.|Bring a picnic next time. Everyone does.|Watch the road past the fork. Bandits, they say."
npc traveller 44 16.4 name="A Traveller" sheet=traveller wander=4 say="Long road from the coast.|The bridge back there's older than the city, they say.|Is it far to the gate? My feet say yes."

trigger watched 17 7 h=18 say="Someone has been watching the road." set=road-ambush

; What the two of you say on the way: setting out, out in the meadow, at the farm, by the stream,
; at the camp (once Brisk has said there are highwaymen, it's their camp), at the fork, on the path
; up to the barrow, far enough short of it to get a word in, and where the wood starts closing in.
trigger bark-road-out 4 15 w=2 h=3 bark=road-out
trigger bark-meadow-out 9 15 w=2 h=3 bark=meadow-out
trigger bark-meadow-farm 5 11 w=4 h=3 bark=meadow-farm
trigger bark-meadow-stream 19 15 w=2 h=3 bark=meadow-stream
trigger bark-road-camp 27 20 w=10 h=6 bark=road-camp
trigger bark-road-camp-bandits 27 20 w=10 h=6 bark=road-camp-bandits
trigger bark-road-fork 37 15 w=5 h=3 bark=road-fork
trigger bark-barrow-mouth 40 7 w=2 h=2 bark=barrow-mouth
trigger bark-meadow-mirewood-edge 50 15 w=2 h=3 bark=meadow-mirewood-edge
